# Context handoff (Auto)

Chat memory ≠ SoT. Thin window / mid-step / new chat → **files win**, never invent NEXT from residual chat.

## SoT (read first every continue / Scout)

1. `active_context.md` — Goal · Core logic · Edge/Fail · Status · paste block
2. `progress.md` — last QA JSON · Next line
3. User's latest message (overrides stale file Status only when explicit)

context-mode `ctx_*`/SQLite ≠ SoT (dump-index only) — on conflict, files win (`context-mode.mdc`).
(1)+(2) contradict latest ask → **stop**, report drift, ask which wins. Do not Builder.

## Hard-stop triggers (no Builder / no "finish the wave")

- User: `context thin` · `handoff only` · `no code` · new chat / continue-from-files
- Long thread + large tool dumps + can't restate DONE/NEXT from files without guessing
- Mid-step and next action needs facts not in files or this turn's results
- `preCompact` hook warn (`.cursor/hooks/precompact-handoff-warn.py`) → treat as thin

On hard-stop: update `active_context.md` (DONE/PARTIAL/NEXT/Out-of-scope + paste block) and `progress.md` Next line → reply with status + paste block only, no new code, no step jump.

## Mid-step partial

| State | Write to `active_context` |
|-------|---------------------------|
| Scout/Architect done | Status = plan ready · NEXT = Builder |
| Builder half-done | PARTIAL = files touched + what's left · NEXT = finish Builder then QA |
| QA incomplete | PARTIAL = checks run/not run · NEXT = QA |
| DevOps notes only | NEXT = user upload/smoke · no fake PASS |

Never mark QA **PASS** without evidence in this turn or `progress.md`.

## New chat / continue paste

Keep a fenced paste under `active_context.md`:
```
Continue <pj> from active_context.md + progress.md.
DONE: … / NEXT: … / SoT + rejects
If context thin: handoff only — no code.
Workflow Scout→… one step per y.
```
New chat turn 1 = Scout from files (or handoff-only). Never skip to Builder.

## Workflow lock

One numerical step per `y` · never Builder+QA same turn as Scout/Architect · `y` after handoff ≠ license to guess NEXT.

## Housekeeping (progress.md self-prune — do at QA/DevOps step AND every Scout, no need to be asked)

`progress.md` holds **pending work only**, not a permanent log: the active task's entry + any earlier entry whose DevOps is still genuinely deferred (not "done and shipped"). When an entry's DevOps completes, or the user explicitly drops/supersedes it, **delete that entry** from `progress.md` in the same turn — don't let finished entries pile up. `active_context.md` always reflects the single current task; overwrite it on a new task, never append.

**Shipped-detection (don't rely on the DevOps line alone):** at every Scout step, before reporting "Scout ပြီးပါပြီ", run `git log --oneline -10` and check each non-active `progress.md` entry's target files/keywords against it. A matching commit = shipped, even if that entry's own DevOps line still says NOT STARTED (formal DevOps notes and an actual commit are different signals — a commit wins). Prune shipped entries silently in the same turn, then report Scout as usual. This check is unconditional — run it whether or not `progress.md` looks stale.

## Reject

Chat-recall implementation when Status/NEXT stale · invented pageKeys/URLs/PASS · scope creep under thin context · `ctx_search` as SoT · replacing this with a Skill · letting `progress.md` accumulate finished-and-shipped entries instead of pruning them.
